flowchart TB
  accTitle: One workspace address, two process generations
  accDescr: Today, a Service can route the same address to replacement workspace B. A serving response alone does not show which process answered. Under the proposal, Compute pins the original workspace A before release, checks A's acknowledgement of the signed release and all four pins, then independently verifies A is serving. On each connection the Gateway verifies TLS with only the pinned CA before sending its bearer. The relay checks the bearer and released original before returning 101. The Gateway checks the generation proof before sending or accepting native frames. Missing or different proof closes the connection.
  subgraph next["Proposed for protected workspaces"]
    direction TB
    pin["Before release: identify A<br/>and pin its workspace binding"] --> ready["Check A acknowledged release;<br/>verify A is serving"]
    ready --> tls["On connect: verify TLS<br/>before sending the bearer"]
    tls --> generation{"Did the upgrade identify<br/>workspace A?"}
    generation -->|Yes| good["Start workspace traffic"]
    generation -->|No| stop["Close before workspace traffic"]
  end
  subgraph now["Today"]
    direction TB
    addr["Same Service address<br/>A is replaced by B"] --> status["Driver returns the address<br/>and reports serving"]
    status --> unknown["Which process answered?<br/>Generation unknown"]
  end
  classDef check fill:#e8f0f7,stroke:#536c85,color:#172c3e
  classDef permit fill:#e5f2e8,stroke:#4c7655,color:#193c23
  classDef refuse fill:#feeee9,stroke:#a45a49,color:#552a21
  class addr,status,unknown,pin,ready,tls,generation check
  class good permit
  class stop refuse
